    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d937">

                <pb facs="0977" n="969" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg969"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">540.61B3/282: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bucknell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-13T19:00:00-05:00">October 13, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>115. Your despatch no. 355 Political, September 21, 1938.<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d937-f1"/> For Everett. Conference on educational films.</p>
                <p>The Department has examined carefully the procès-verbal, the final act, and your
                    report. The procès-verbal and the final act are acceptable to the Department and
                    you are authorized to sign them at <pb facs="0978" n="970" xml:id="pg970"/> the
                    convenience of the Secretariat of the League of Nations,<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d937-f2"/> making “under the terms of Article IV of this
                    procès-verbal” the same reservation that was made to the Convention of
                        1933.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d937-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d937-f1" n="7" xml:id="d937-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d937-f2" n="8" xml:id="d937-f2-content">
                <p>Mr. Everett informed the Department in despatch No. 398 Political, October 18,
                    that he signed the procès-verbal and the final act on October 17 (540.61B3/287).
                    The texts of the acts are printed in League of Nations Treaty Series, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">cxcviii</hi>, p. 111.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d937-f3" n="9" xml:id="d937-f3-content">
                <p>The reservation made to article XX of the Convention of October 11, 1933, stated
                    that the United States assumed no obligation in respect of the Philippine
                    Islands, the Virgin Islands, American Samoa, or Guam.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
